[67.0293, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ the committed spec builds clean and writes exactly the committed files \u001b[90m(4107.93375ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ an animation longer than X lets a card start by itself is refused \u001b[90m(1487.221083ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a title longer than X shows is refused, not cut \u001b[90m(768.289ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a tab the page has no pane for is refused \u001b[90m(2380.081958ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ the player is served over https or not at all \u001b[90m(1136.682125ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a backend the compiler does not emit is refused \u001b[90m(335.69375ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a command with no handler, or a handler with no command, is refused \u001b[90m(1586.305208ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a phrase the spec defines and the terminal never says, or says and the spec lacks, is refused \u001b[90m(1471.2115ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a card demo too long to type inside the box, or inside X's autoplay limit, is refused \u001b[90m(2256.254333ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ every backend has a share page whose player opens the terminal on that backend, and gi"]
[67.0527, "o", "t keeps it \u001b[90m(2615.170167ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ every terminal command runs on hello_world and says only what the spec lets it say \u001b[90m(2619.757ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ run prints the command for a machine with rustc and never a result; js is imported here \u001b[90m(123.609208ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[67.1245, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ t27c gen-rust is t27c gen rust; gcc, an unknown t27c subcommand and a typo each say why \u001b[90m(622.771584ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[67.2098, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ save asks for a download of exactly what the compiler emitted \u001b[90m(301.890041ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[67.3108, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ site.js is built from the site source, so a palette change there reaches the player \u001b[90m(2299.577791ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ the spec highlighter: a /* inside a string opens no comment, and a ; line is prose \u001b[90m(227.974375ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ hello_world: gen-verilog emits what a Verilog-2005 reader refuses, and the struct packs to 25 \u001b[90m(599.484ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ hello_world: the HIR backend writes an unescaped `config` port 32 bits wide for a 25-bit struct \u001b[90m(7.999167ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a \"/*\" inside a Verilog string opens no comment, so what follows still counts \u001b[90m(0.342959ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a task is declared, and `function real` names its result type, not the function \u001b[90m(13.066042ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[67.3837, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ an array sized by a constant packs the way t27c packs it \u001b[90m(42.499209ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
